One Way TLS: 
  • Broker has a certificate
  • Clients verify the broker's identity
  • Clients don't need their own certificates
  • This is how most websites work — you verify the bank is real, but the bank doesn't verify you via certificate

Mutual TLS
  • Both broker and the clients have certificates
  • Everyone verifies everyone
  • "Only sensors with valid certificates can connect"



